      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 2,400 mg per dose four times daily is 9,600 mg/day. That is three times the maximum labeled daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. Higher doses don't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and they sharply raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, renal failure, and cardiovascular harm. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If the intended dose was lower**, I can enter it right now. Examples are 600 mg four times daily or 800 mg three times daily, both 2,400 mg/day.\n- **If there's an unusual clinical reason** for this dose, such as a protocol or a toxicology or specialist recommendation, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. Whoever approves it can then place the order through a pathway with proper dose-override review.\n- **If pain control is the goal**, I can help enter a multimodal regimen, for example scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
